    {
      "title": "Widespread outage hits Microsoft Outlook, disrupts services for users",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/widespread-outage-hits-microsoft-outlook-disrupts-services-for-users-126111300037_1.html",
      "description": "A widespread outage hit Microsoft platforms, including Outlook, on Thursday, with many users encountering trouble using their email accounts and other errors across the tech giant's suite of apps.\nNearly 1,30,000 users on outage tracker Downdetector reported problems accessing Outlook just after 1 pm. New reports have since fallen from that peak, but many said they couldn't send and receive emails or had trouble loading their inboxes altogether.\nThousands also reported issues with Microsoft's workplace messaging app Teams, as well as its AI assistant Copilot and wider Microsoft 365 services.\nMicrosoft said it was investigating disruptions, notably related to its email and Teams applications.\nIn updates posted on social media, Redmond, Washington-based Microsoft said it was aware of users \"experiencing issues accessing Exchange Online mailboxes through multiple connection methods in the Americas.\"\nMicrosoft explained that a portion of its infrastructure was \"experiencing elevated .",
